#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186073495 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186073684 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "6ffe13c6-a2b6-5d70-8ebe-d152ae4db35f" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying a Multiplication Problem Corresponding to a Model"}] :question/id #uuid "f26ed088-6f0b-56b8-9027-9b9af4bcf415" :question/math-academy-id "e-14484" :question/problem "![](images/4f/4f5bfdd38a8c02510e86279ac548a2a6b889f9eb33a8ef8c273fd2e384e54b72.png)\n\nWhat multiplication problem is represented by the model above?" :question/worked-solution "We have\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{1}{3}\n$$\n\non the left and\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{1}{6}\n$$\n\non the right.\n\n![](images/b4/b43d5a0e0a44e6d418a901dc9fa806079b1b9425fc111640439e4338f8bf0d84.png)\n\nTherefore, the multiplication problem shown is:\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{1}{3} \\times \\dfrac{1}{2} = \\dfrac{1}{6}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186073498 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186073685 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3f3ddce4-2cf8-5bf6-86d3-8c304ee6c241" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying a Missing Number in a Model"}] :question/id #uuid "a653f45f-e638-5646-a55c-13b319e511b0" :question/math-academy-id "e-14490" :question/problem "What number is missing from the multiplication problem below?\n\n![](images/69/69f859c61c693f7ece01fef8f829fdc772acae77e90be97b7b093fb9849acc95.png)" :question/worked-solution "We have\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{1}{2}\n$$\n\non the left and\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{1}{6}\n$$\n\non the right.\n\n![](images/dc/dcb89325ddd68043c9edf2f595a7a7d89b3ba078bbb1805af7bea58867f627b6.png)\n\nThe shape on the right-hand side is split into $\\color{blue}3$ equal parts by horizontal lines. So, the shaded part on the left is $\\color{blue}3$ times larger than the shaded part on the right.\n\nTherefore, the multiplication problem shown is:\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{1}{2} \\times \\dfrac{1}{\\color{blue}{3}} = \\dfrac{1}{6}\n$$\n\nSo, the missing number is $\\color{blue}3$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186073499 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186073686 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "0bd1c12d-acb6-5961-a248-47f172fe5bef" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying a Model Corresponding to a Multiplication Problem"}] :question/id #uuid "9bc02e5b-5028-5aa1-85d8-c1217b425c36" :question/math-academy-id "e-14491" :question/problem "What picture is missing from the multiplication model below?\n\n![](images/39/39c8668bd4bf5309b708769a99d9d3fa2184f0937411d437de8a1195853e5118.png)" :question/worked-solution "In the model, we have\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{1}{4}\n$$\n\non the left.\n\nSince we are multiplying by\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{1}{\\color{blue}5}\n$$\n\n, we need to split the whole into $\\color{blue}5$ equal parts horizontally.\n\n![](images/65/6584c694fbbc990dfa3b58a19545d3deb9889f162da6e02a9820310a190ae04e.png)\n\nFrom the picture on the right, we obtain that the shaded part represents\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{1}{20}\n$$\n\nof the whole.\n\nThe missing picture is:\n\n![](images/e3/e349233ebb5e3927f0d4bda98cb2470c1f17574a522d2f4b9cbddaf365fe946d.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186073500 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186073687 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "16e2265e-5c75-538f-91a1-9120d2f77c9e" :knowledge-point/title "Multiplying a Fraction by a Unit Fraction Using a Model"}] :question/id #uuid "4730b433-9614-58ea-a452-e404c237ba3b" :question/math-academy-id "e-14492" :question/problem "![](images/82/82439d51448a442dede4b3965ecbbd2f2daa7b2365ea75c80951478fd10af65c.png)\n\nUse the model above to calculate $\\dfrac{4}{5} \\times \\dfrac{1}{3}$." :question/worked-solution "Since we need to multiply by\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{1}{\\color{blue}3}\n$$\n\n, we split the whole into $\\color{blue}3$ equal parts horizontally.\n\n![](images/a9/a95b378064e6ec2ed15637fd05ea49e5f988bfb30d8ae788a7b2086ff920a65f.png)\n\nFrom the picture on the right, we obtain that the shaded part represents\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{4}{15}\n$$\n\nof the whole.\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{4}{5} \\times \\dfrac{1}{3} = \\dfrac{4}{15}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186074420 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186073687 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "16e2265e-5c75-538f-91a1-9120d2f77c9e" :knowledge-point/title "Multiplying a Fraction by a Unit Fraction Using a Model"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a3492c6e-0cf3-5ffe-b75c-9c4617fd3274" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{12}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186072759} {:answer/id #uuid "df482a0e-f324-5349-b382-8fe5574bc67a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{12}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186072760} {:answer/id #uuid "f9903a21-0217-58f2-8d63-41d105a30c08" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186072761} {:answer/id #uuid "223379f8-ee6a-5c47-8bd1-f452e3187e1b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186072762} {:answer/id #uuid "712639d1-5da2-5392-8851-f92f6c470e4e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186072763}] :answer-field/id #uuid "66fc3948-4f7b-51cd-b723-f43fedc0d1be" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186072758}] :question/id #uuid "d8028372-de90-5318-b125-be12ab64e3cc" :question/math-academy-id "q-60224" :question/problem "![](images/7d/7d2474d5fd25cbb23c534e4d8f67726177988a49f9c0e271b91b0ff677dabd41.png)\n\nUse the model above to calculate $\\frac{2}{3} \\cdot \\frac{1}{4}$."}]}
